    faq: [
      { q: "What is Himalayan Brothers Hotels?", a: "Himalayan Brothers Hotels is a family-run group of five hotels in Himachal Pradesh: Buddha House and Quartz near the Norbulingka Institute in Dharamshala, Samdupling in Mohli, Spiti Villa near Kaza in Spiti, and Diwan Sachpass near Sach Pass in Chamba. Divyansh Sood rebuilt the group's website in Astro in 2026." },
      { q: "How do guests book a room on the site?", a: "One booking form covers all five hotels. For Quartz and Spiti Villa it opens their booking engines; for Buddha House, Samdupling and Diwan it opens WhatsApp with the stay already written out. It still works without JavaScript." },
      { q: "What happened to the old website's URLs?", a: "Every hotel page kept its exact old URL. Old per-room pages redirect permanently to anchors on their hotel's page, retired slugs point to their current pages, and the bare domain redirects to www in a single hop." },
      { q: "Why doesn't the site show star ratings in Google results?", a: "Because Google treats review markup that a business publishes about itself as self-serving and won't show stars for it. The site shows each hotel's Google and Tripadvisor rating to people, with the date it was checked, but adds no review markup. Unverifiable ratings and six untraceable reviews from the old site were removed." },
      { q: "How fast is the hotel group's website?", a: "At launch Lighthouse scored 98–100 for mobile performance on all 12 pages tested and 100 for accessibility, best practices and SEO, with LCP between 1.7 and 2.3 seconds. Desktop scored 100, and axe found no accessibility violations across 19 pages." },
      { q: "Is the travel site himalayanbrothers.com the same business?", a: "Yes. It is the same family's travel desk, run from Hotel Buddha House, and it was built on this site's design system. Its structured data references these hotels' own identifiers so the two sites read as one business." },
    ],
